{{Quote|So you're part of the Mining Guild, then?"<br />"No, not actually. Our operation is small enough not to be noticed, which is advantageous for everybody since our customers are anxious to avoid attracting attention to themselves.|[[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] and [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]], regarding Cloud City|<ref name="Episode V">{{Film|V}}</ref>}}
The '''Mining Guild''', also known as the '''Galactic Mining Guild''', was a powerful network of [[miner]]s that [[Mining|harvested]] and controlled natural resources throughout [[the galaxy]]. Initially a part of the [[Commerce Guild]], it was aligned with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]] before collaborating with [[Galactic Empire]] during its [[Imperial Era|reign]].

==History==
===Creation and Clone Wars===
The Mining Guild's early strongholds included [[Planet|worlds]] like [[Empress Teta]], a significant supplier of [[carbonite]] with ties to early hyperspace exploration. Through the exploitation (and sometimes, the instigation) of interplanetary upheaval, the guild expanded its influence over several millennia, eventually growing to control [[the galaxy]]'s resources.<ref name="NoP" /> [[Desler Gizh Outworld Mobility Corporation]] was part of the guild.<ref name="Land, Sea and Air Speeders">{{EncyclopediaCite|Speeders on Land, Sea, and Air (1)}}</ref> The guild eventually became a part of the [[Commerce Guild]].<ref name="Rise of the Separatists" />

By the start of the [[Clone Wars]], the Mining Guild exerted control over the [[Tetan monarchy]]<ref name="NoP" /> and dominated billions of young, nameless, metal-rich [[planet]]s in the spiral arms of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref> Along with various other galactic conglomerates, including the Commerce Guild, the Mining Guild chose to side against the [[Galactic Republic]] and with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], forcing its member worlds such as Empress Teta to follow in its footsteps.<ref name="NoP" /> After the Separatists were [[Mission to Mustafar|defeated]] and the Republic [[Proclamation of the New Order|transitioned]] into the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> the guild escaped Imperial reprisals by swearing fealty to [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]].<ref name="NoP" />

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Fuel thieves. Alert our sentries. Protect the shipment at all costs!|Yushyn|audio=Yushyn-Fuel_Thieves.flac|<ref name="The Call">{{Rebels|The Call}}</ref>}}
During the [[Imperial Era]], the Mining Guild openly collaborated with the [[Galactic Empire]], offering raw materials to the Imperial war machine at discounted prices.<ref name="NoP" /> In exchange, the guild was permitted to use a modified [[TIE/mg Mining Guild starfighter|variant]] of the Imperial [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE/ln starfighter]].<ref name="DB MG Fighter">{{Databank|mining-guild-tie-fighter|Mining Guild TIE fighter}}</ref> The guild was also able to maintain control over its own mining operations instead of losing that control to the Empire.<ref name="Episode V" /> The Mining Guild protected [[spice]] [[mining]] on the planet [[Kessel]], the origin point for most of [[the galaxy]]'s spice supply.<ref name="209 Spice">{{InsiderCite|209|Spice: Just Say No!}}</ref> The mines themselves were worked by [[Slavery|slaves]] of the [[Pyke Syndicate]]<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> or Empire, which also played a role in Kessel security.<ref name="Spark of Rebellion">{{Rebels|Spark of Rebellion}}</ref>

[[File:Asteroid_Belt_Gas_Refinery.jpg|thumb|left|270px|The Clouzon-36 gas refinery]]
In [[3 BBY]],<ref name="The Call date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[The Call]]" to [[3 BBY]].</ref> the Guild ran an [[Asteroid Belt Gas Refinery]] located on a [[Unidentified planetoid (Mining Guild)|small planetoid]], where they extracted [[Clouzon-36]] gas. However, that facility was discovered by the [[Spectres]], a crew of anti-Empire freedom fighters, who stole its fuel for the rebellion and destroyed the complex.<ref name="The Call" /> Despite the loss of that Clouzon-36 refinery, the Mining Guild remained powerful.<ref name="DB MG" />

The Mining Guild sent [[Agents of the Mining Guild|agents]] to patrol and represent its interests in the [[Spice mines of Kessel|spice mines]] on Kessel in order to make sure the it got its cut of the profits.<ref name="Solo Guide">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref> In [[10 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{FilmDate|Solo}}</ref> agent [[Yorsh Manted]]<ref name="Solo Guide" /> was present during the [[Raid on Kessel]] and ensuing slave revolt.<ref name="Solo" />

The Mining Guild regularly patrolled the [[Sereeda Waypoint]], a [[hyperspace waypoint]] located in their claims territory.<ref name="Steps" /> In [[2 BBY]],<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[Steps Into Shadow]]" to [[2 BBY]].</ref> the Spectres once again clashed with the Guild, this time in the Sereeda, as they had to momentarily come out of [[hyperspace]] there and recalculate their jump. The Guild deployed two TIEs and demanded the rebels pay the hyperspace toll, however the Spectres destroyed the fighters and jumped back into hyperspace.<ref name="Steps" />

[[File:Mining_Guild_Surveyor_XW2.png|thumb|right|250px|A Mining Guild surveyor piloting a TIE/mg starfighter.]]
After being rejected by the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] and the [[Grand Hutt Council]], [[General]] [[Davits Draven]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Alliance]] wrote to [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]] about being potential allies with the Mining Guild, claiming, that while the Mining Guild operated under the Empire, it was more of a convenient relationship, not an ideological one. At the time of the later, the Alliance was investigating Mining Guild operations on [[Ord Mantell]], [[Raxus Prime]], [[The Wheel]], [[Vergesso Prime|Vergesso]], the [[Ring of Kafrene]], [[Smuggler's Run]], [[Takodana]], and [[Nar Shaddaa]].<ref name="Rebel Files" />

[[Cloud City]], a [[tibanna]] gas mining operation in the [[atmosphere]] of the [[planet]] [[Bespin]], was able to keep its activities small and avoid being part of the Empire or the Mining Guild. This was to the advantage of its customers, who did not want to gain attention.<ref name="Episode V" />

===Era of the Resistance===
{{Quote|That is the moon of Kyzring. It's loaded with carnium, an energy-rich metal that powers half this sector. The Mining Guild has been digging into this moon for years. They take what they can use, and whatever's left, well&hellip;you see for yourself.|Poe Dameron, to Rey|<ref name="Squad Goals" />}}
[[File:Moon_of_Kyzring.jpg|thumb|left|150px|The guild had been mining the moon of Kyzring for years.]]
By the rise of the [[First Order]] and the creation of the [[Resistance]], the Mining Guild was still active, and, according to the Resistance, was not what it once was. [[Vice Admiral]] [[Amilyn Holdo]] believed that this allowed the stronger possibility that the Mining Guild would accept a partnership with the Resistance.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

By the time following the [[Battle of Crait]] during the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the First Order and Resistance, the guild had been mining the [[moon of Kyzring]], which was rich with [[carnium]], for [[Standard year|years]]. The guild would take what it could use, and [[Poe Dameron]] recounted this information to fellow Resistance member [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] while on a training mission.<ref name="Squad Goals" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|Those TIEs have been modified. They're not Imperial.''"<br />"''Well, they're acting like it.|[[Sabine Wren]] and [[Kanan Jarrus]]|<ref name="The Call" />}}
[[File:MiningGuildSentry-SWZ.png|thumb|right|270px|A Mining Guild used ''Aurore''-class freighters and TIE/mg fighters to patrol their territory.]]
Thanks to its association with the Empire, the Guild was allowed to use a special [[TIE/mg Mining Guild starfighter|variant]] of the Imperial [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighter]] modified with a yellow color scheme and 2 notches out of the wings.<ref name="DB MG Fighter">{{Databank|mining-guild-tie-fighter|Mining Guild TIE fighter}}</ref> For more security purposes, the Mining Guild also used yellow [[YV-865 Aurore-class freighter|''Aurore''-class freighters]]<ref name="Steps" /> and [[X4 Gunship]]s.<ref name="Rebel Files" /> On [[Lothal]]<ref name="Crawler Commandeers" /> in around [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Chronology Note">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[Heroes of Mandalore]]" to [[1 BBY]].</ref> the Mining Guild utilized [[ore crawler]]s for the scouring of the terrain for raw materials,<ref name="Crawler Commandeers" /> as well as [[Mining Guild excavation driller]]s for large scale operations.<ref name="AWBW">{{Rebels|A World Between Worlds}}</ref> For security on the crawlers, yellow [[IG-RM bodyguard and enforcer droid|IG-RM droids]] with weak [[Audio sensor|audio receptors]] were used.<ref name="DB MG Security Droid">{{Databank|mining-guild-security-droid|Mining Guild Security Droid}}</ref> The Mining Guild also used [[phase connector]]s.<ref name="Dangerous Business">{{Resistance|Dangerous Business}}</ref>

